# MyJarbis
# `**/` on purpose: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to this
# directory, so the old `.myjarbis/memory.db` only matched the repo root.
# Any stray brain created in a subdirectory stayed untracked-but-visible —
# and there are two in this checkout, left by the bug where every command
# created a DB wherever it ran (fixed in v0.3: only `init` creates one).
**/.myjarbis/memory.db
**/.myjarbis/memory.db-journal
**/.myjarbis/memory.db-wal
**/.myjarbis/memory.db-shm
# `myjarbis migrate` backs the brain up next to itself as
# memory.db.pre-v4.<timestamp>, with its own -wal and -shm. The patterns
# above name the SQLite sidecars exactly, so none of them catch a backup.
**/.myjarbis/memory.db.*
.claude/skills/myjarbis-*/

# The rest of what `init` materializes here. MyJarbis manages its own repo
# (we dogfood it), so these are this machine's generated output, not source:
# the commands come from global/templates/.claude/commands/jarbis.<lang>.md,
# and `active` is written by `module use`. Versioning them would ship one
# developer's language choice and selected module to everyone.
# settings.local.json is also the local-override half of Claude Code's
# settings pair — and it holds absolute paths naming real client projects,
# which this public repo must never carry (same rule as the docs/ block).
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/commands/jarbis*.md
.myjarbis/active

# MyJarbis v0.1 legacy artifacts (regenerated by myjarbis-init,
# never edited by contributors of THIS repo).
.myjarbis/bin/
.myjarbis/context/
.myjarbis/prompts/

# MyJarbis
.myjarbis/context/codebase.txt

# Local operational notes — machine-specific, and they name real projects.
# docs/ holds both tracked docs and untracked working notes; these are the
# untracked kind and must stay that way: this repo is public, and the rule
# is that no client or private project name ever lands in it.
docs/MIGRATION-v0.3.md
docs/HOW-IT-WORKS.md
docs/SESSION-*.md
docs/COMPARISON-*.md

# Install artifacts a dev run leaves in the checkout. global/bin shadows
# bin/ (see the guard in tests/run-all.sh); .source records an install path.
global/bin/
global/.source
